---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import Text from "@components/core/Text.astro"
import { Pages } from "@utils"
import PartnerFooter from "@components/PartnerFooter.astro"
---

<Layout title="Tennibot vs. Spinshot | Tennibot" showFooter={false} showHeader={false} showPartnerHeader={true} showSecondaryHeader={false} showSecondaryMenu={false}>
    <main class="bg-t-off-black overflow-hidden text-t-off-white" >
        <section class="w-[80%] mx-auto mt-36 mb-24" >
            <Text tag="h1" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-center md:text-4xl text-2xl mb-10" >Tennibot Partner vs. Spinshot: What You Need to Know</Text>
        </section>

        <section class="w-[80%] mx-auto" >
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Before we dive into the comparison, I want to establish that Spinshot is a solid traditional ball machine with a long track record. That said, here are some of the differences between their machines and the Tennibot.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                1. Mobility Matters — Static Machine vs. Autonomous Movement
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                <span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >Spinshot</span> machines are static. That means if you want to practice a variety of shots—say, a down-the-line forehand, then an inside-out forehand, then a wide-angle cross—you’ll need to physically move the machine every time, tweak the settings, and hope the angles match what you need. <br /><span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >Tennibot Partner?</span> Fully mobile and intelligent. It moves autonomously across the court, dynamically adjusting angles and positioning to create realistic, full-court training sequences—without you lifting a finger.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                2. Vision-Driven Intelligence vs. Blind Launching
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                <span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >Spinshot</span> machines don’t “see” the court. They don’t know where the player is, where the net is, or how the ball is interacting with the environment. No cameras, no real-time tracking, no adaptability. <br/>
                <span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >Tennibot Partner</span> is powered by a vision system built for elite-level training. It uses synchronized 4K cameras and proprietary algorithms to track court lines, player positioning, and lighting conditions—delivering consistent, intelligent drills that adapt to the way you play.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                3. Smarter Workflow, Simpler Experience
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Adjusting drills on <span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >Spinshot</span> often involves knobs, remote controls, and trial-and-error setups. The machine has no context about the drill or the player—it just launches balls.
                <br /><br />With Tennibot, you control everything from your phone. The mobile app lets you define shot patterns, intensity, and ball frequency with a few taps. Want to change drills mid-session? No problem—just tap and go.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                4. Built with Safety in mind
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                <span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >The Tennibot Partner</span> is designed with safety as a top priority, unlike the <span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >Spinshot</span> ball machine, which, to our knowledge, lacks any cameras or visible obstacle or human detection sensors.
                <br /><br /><span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >The Tennibot Partner</span> is equipped with five advanced ultrasonic sensors and cameras that detect people and obstacles in real time. It automatically pauses its operation to avoid accidents. This multilayer safety approach ensures a safer training environment for players and coaches. This makes the Tennibot Partner a more intelligent and more responsible choice for parents or users concerned about safety.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                Final Thoughts
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                <span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >Spinshot</span> machines helped define an earlier era of tennis training.<br/>But if you’re looking for intelligent, mobile, vision-powered performance that adapts to your game—not the other way around—<span class="font-avenirBold text-t-off-white" >Tennibot Partner is the future</span>.
            </Text>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>
<PartnerFooter />